    (difficulty . "0.188"))
  ((question . "A hot spring produces water at a temperature of 56°C. The water flows into a large lake, with a mean temperature of 14°C, at a rate of 0.1 m³ of water per min. What is the rate of working of an ideal heat engine which uses all the available energy?")
    (answer . "37.3")
    (domain . "physics")
    (difficulty . "0.25"))
  ((question . "An automotive engine weighing 240 kg is supported on four springs with linear characteristics. Each of the front two springs has a stiffness of 16 MN/m, while the stiffness of each rear spring is 32 MN/m. Determine the engine speed (in rpm) at which resonance is likely to occur.")
    (answer . "6040")
    (domain . "physics")
    (difficulty . "0.188"))
  ((question . "1.2 m³ of air is heated reversibly at constant pressure from 300 K to 600 K, and is then cooled reversibly at constant volume back to the initial temperature of 300 K. Given the initial pressure is 1 bar, \\( c_p = 1.005 \\, \\text{kJ/kg K} \\), and \\( R = 0.287 \\, \\text{kJ/kg K} \\), calculate:  \n(i) The net heat flow.  \n(ii) The overall change in entropy.")
    (answer . "0.2773")
    (domain . "physics")
    (difficulty . "0.375"))
  ((question . "What is the expected intensity of the M+6 peak (relative to the M⁺ peak) for the molecule C₆H₆O₂Cl₂, where M⁺ is the molecular ion and M+6 is the isotopic peak with six additional mass units?")
    (answer . "3.4%")
