  ((question . "For the reaction \\( \\text{C}_6\\text{H}_5\\text{N(CH}_3\\text{)}_2 + \\text{CH}_3\\text{I} \\rightarrow \\text{C}_6\\text{H}_5\\text{N(CH}_3\\text{)}_2^+ + \\text{I}^- \\), which is first order in each reactant, the rate constant at 24.8°C is \\( 8.39 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{ L mol}^{-1} \\text{ s}^{-1} \\). If both reactants have initial concentrations of 0.100 mol L\\(^{-1}\\), find the time required for 75% of the reactants to react at 24.8°C. Assume the reverse reaction is negligible.")
