  ((question . "A 45-year-old woman presents with dyspnea on exertion (DOE) and paroxysmal atrial fibrillation (AF). She has a fixed split S2 on exam with a 2/6 systolic ejection murmur (SEM) at the left sternal border (LSB). Echocardiogram shows:\n- Dilated right ventricle (RV) and right atrium (RA), normal left ventricle (LV)\n- Secundum atrial septal defect (ASD)\n- Pulmonary artery (PA) systolic pressure of 70 mmHg\n\nThe following are found at catheterization:\n- Saturations (%): IVC, 70; SVC, 67; RA, 82; RV, 87; PA, 88; LV, 98; aorta, 98; femoral artery (FA), 98\n- Pressures (mmHg): PA, 70/50; FA, 120/70; pulmonary capillary wedge pressure (PCWP), 10\n- Total cardiac output (TCO), 6.0 L/min\n\nWhat is the pulmonary-to-systemic blood flow ratio (Qp/Qs)?")
    (answer . "1.6")
    (domain . "biology")
    (difficulty . "0.125"))
